# Who may do what, by the name in the client's certificate (ADR-0017).

# The Gateway reads every edge's samples and writes each edge's configuration: what an edge reads
# is derived in the cloud and delivered to it, never typed into the edge by hand (ADR-0019).
user scada-gateway
topic read scada/edge/+/samples
topic write scada/edge/+/config

# Every edge writes its own samples topic and reads its own configuration, and nothing else: %u is
# the name in its certificate, which is its Edge:Id. An edge that publishes under another edge's
# name, or reads another edge's configuration, is refused here, and the refusal is written to the
# audit file.
pattern write scada/edge/%u/samples
pattern read scada/edge/%u/config
